{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,24]],"date-time":"2026-09-24T15:48:00Z","timestamp":1790264880322,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":46,"publisher":"MDPI AG","issue":"2","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2021,1,14]],"date-time":"2021-01-14T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1610582400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/100000002","name":"National Institutes of Health","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["R15GM120702"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["R15GM120702"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100000002","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["IJMS"],"abstract":"<jats:p>The binding of vascular endothelial growth factor A (VEGF) to VEGF receptor-2 (VEGFR-2) stimulates angiogenic signaling. Lipid rafts are cholesterol-dense regions of the plasma membrane that serve as an organizational platform for biomolecules. Although VEGFR2 has been shown to colocalize with lipid rafts to regulate its activation, the effect of lipid rafts on non-activated VEGFR2 has not been explored. Here, we characterized the involvement of lipid rafts in modulating the stability of non-activated VEGFR2 in endothelial cells using raft disrupting agents: methyl-\u03b2-cyclodextrin, sphingomyelinase and simvastatin. Disrupting lipid rafts selectively decreased the levels of non-activated VEGFR2 as a result of increased lysosomal degradation. The decreased expression of VEGFR2 translated to reduced VEGF-activation of the extracellular signal-regulated protein kinases (ERK). Overall, our results indicate that lipid rafts stabilize VEGFR2 and its associated signal transduction activities required for angiogenesis. Thus, modulation of lipid rafts may provide a means to regulate the sensitivity of endothelial cells to VEGF stimulation. Indeed, the ability of simvastatin to down regulate VEGFR2 and inhibit VEGF activity suggest a potential mechanism underlying the observation that this drug improves outcomes in the treatment of certain cancers.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3390\/ijms22020798","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2021,1,14]],"date-time":"2021-01-14T11:39:14Z","timestamp":1610624354000},"page":"798","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3390\/mdpi_crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":40,"title":["Lipid Raft Association Stabilizes VEGF Receptor 2 in Endothelial Cells"],"prefix":"10.3390","volume":"22","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2444-635X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Ibukunoluwapo O.","family":"Zabroski","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Biological Sciences, University of Massachusetts Lowell, Lowell, MA 01854, USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7290-5616","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Matthew A.","family":"Nugent","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Biological Sciences, University of Massachusetts Lowell, Lowell, MA 01854, USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"1968","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2021,1,14]]},"reference":[{"key":"ref_1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"932","DOI":"10.1038\/nature04478","article-title":"Angiogenesis in life, disease and medicine","volume":"438","author":"Carmeliet","year":"2005","journal-title":"Nature"},{"key":"ref_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"937","DOI":"10.1038\/nature04479","article-title":"Endothelial cells and VEGF in vascular development","volume":"438","author":"Coultas","year":"2005","journal-title":"Nature"},{"key":"ref_3","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"347","DOI":"10.1007\/s12079-016-0352-8","article-title":"VEGF-A\/VEGFR2 signaling network in endothelial cells relevant to angiogenesis","volume":"10","author":"Abhinand","year":"2016","journal-title":"J. Cell Commun. Signal."},{"key":"ref_4","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"915","DOI":"10.1002\/iub.234","article-title":"Structure and function of VEGF receptors","volume":"61","author":"Stuttfeld","year":"2009","journal-title":"Iubmb Life"},{"key":"ref_5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"16892","DOI":"10.1074\/jbc.M116.730309","article-title":"Constitutive Endocytosis of VEGFR2 Protects the Receptor against Shedding","volume":"291","author":"Basagiannis","year":"2016","journal-title":"J. Biol. Chem."},{"key":"ref_6","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"e75833","DOI":"10.1371\/journal.pone.0075833","article-title":"Microtubules coordinate VEGFR2 signaling and sorting","volume":"8","author":"Czeisler","year":"2013","journal-title":"PLoS ONE"},{"key":"ref_7","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"31","DOI":"10.1038\/35036052","article-title":"Lipid rafts and signal transduction","volume":"1","author":"Simons","year":"2000","journal-title":"Nat. Rev. Mol. Cell Biol."},{"key":"ref_8","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"655","DOI":"10.1194\/jlr.R200021-JLR200","article-title":"Lipid rafts: Bringing order to chaos","volume":"44","author":"Pike","year":"2003","journal-title":"J. Lipid Res."},{"key":"ref_9","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"219","DOI":"10.1042\/bj20031348","article-title":"Isolation and characterization of lipid rafts with different properties from RBL-2H3 (rat basophilic leukaemia) cells","volume":"380","author":"Radeva","year":"2004","journal-title":"Biochem. J."},{"key":"ref_10","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"4783","DOI":"10.1091\/mbc.e03-06-0354","article-title":"Gangliosides that associate with lipid rafts mediate transport of cholera and related toxins from the plasma membrane to endoplasmic reticulm","volume":"14","author":"Fujinaga","year":"2003","journal-title":"Mol. Biol. Cell"},{"key":"ref_11","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1357","DOI":"10.1089\/ars.2008.2365","article-title":"Lipid rafts and caveolae and their role in compartmentation of redox signaling","volume":"11","author":"Patel","year":"2009","journal-title":"Antioxid. Redox Signal."},{"key":"ref_12","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1099","DOI":"10.1242\/jcs.01681","article-title":"Lipid rafts and membrane dynamics","volume":"118","author":"Rajendran","year":"2005","journal-title":"J. Cell Sci."},{"key":"ref_13","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1537","DOI":"10.1007\/s00018-014-1814-x","article-title":"Lipid rafts: Integrated platforms for vascular organization offering therapeutic opportunities","volume":"72","author":"Laurenzana","year":"2015","journal-title":"Cell Mol. Life Sci."},{"key":"ref_14","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"331","DOI":"10.1042\/bj20031082","article-title":"Heparan sulphate proteoglycans modulate fibroblast growth factor-2 binding through a lipid raft-mediated mechanism","volume":"379","author":"Chu","year":"2004","journal-title":"Biochem. J."},{"key":"ref_15","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"89","DOI":"10.1146\/annurev.pharmtox.45.120403.095748","article-title":"Pleiotropic effects of statins","volume":"45","author":"Liao","year":"2005","journal-title":"Annu. Rev. Pharmacol. Toxicol."},{"key":"ref_16","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"554","DOI":"10.4103\/2230-8210.163106","article-title":"Pleiotropic effects of statins","volume":"19","author":"Kavalipati","year":"2015","journal-title":"Indian J. Endocrinol. Metab."},{"key":"ref_17","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"603","DOI":"10.1517\/14740331003662620","article-title":"Statin use and cancer risk: A comprehensive review","volume":"9","author":"Boudreau","year":"2010","journal-title":"Expert Opin. Drug Saf."},{"key":"ref_18","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"516","DOI":"10.3389\/fchem.2020.00516","article-title":"The Innovative Potential of Statins in Cancer: New Targets for New Therapies